  "body": "Follows #3464. The usage ledger now keeps a call whose vendor counts no cache (Kiro: a plugin's `magpie_cache_unknown`) as one. Every hit rate built on `usage.Totals` leaves that call out.\n\nHit rates read from agents' own session files don't. `sessions.Tokens` has no such flag, and a Claude Code session file records Kiro's 0 cache read like any other:\n\n- TUI Sessions: `internal/tui/sessions.go:333`, `(N% hit)`\n- CLI: `internal/cli/sessions_cli.go:422`, `hitRate`\n- GUI Usage → Sessions totals tile (`plugins/usage/page.js`, about line 2645)\n\nEach shows a rate only when CacheRead > 0, so a Kiro-only session shows none. A session that mixes Kiro with a vendor that counts its cache is diluted, though: its Kiro prompt counts as missed.\n\nA fix would carry the flag through `sessions.Tokens`, or join gateway rows to session calls. About 120 positional `sessions.Tokens{...}` literals in the tests make a field addition a wide change. That is why #3464's fix left it alone.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
