   "body": "Delivered on `fix/issue-batch-1025a` ([fe330ea1](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/fe330ea1), skygunner's fork): `sessions.Tokens` carries `CacheUnknown` now — the prompt tokens of calls whose vendor counted no cache — and every hit rate that reads Tokens leaves them out of its denominator, on Totals' rule (#3464): the TUI's and CLI's \"(N% hit)\" and the Usage page's Sessions totals tile.\n\nThe gateway projections sum it from the records (GatewaySession, its days and models), so a session seen only through the gateway shows its true rate. A session the agent also keeps a file of was told zeros in that file, so its list row (`/api/sessions`) joins the amount back from the one kept projection — `usage.NativeSessionUnknown`, read from the cached projection, no extra log pass.\n\nRed before, the dilution you described: a session with one Kiro call (cache_unknown, prompt 900) and one counted call (100 read of a 1,100 prompt) showed 45% — 900 of 2,000; after, 81%. The field addition took the positional `Tokens{...}` literals in the sessions tests from five values to six (126 sites, all `, 0` — the wide change that held #3464 back is mechanical after all).\n\nStill open, said in the commit and in `provider-plugins.md`: a native session's per-day rows inside `Stats.Days` — what the totals tile sums for that session — still count the unknown prompt as a miss. That join needs the day level; the field is there for it now.\n\nRun: `go test ./internal/sessions ./internal/usage` (1,157 ok), `-tags nogui ./internal/gui ./internal/tui ./internal/cli` (826 ok), sessions-overview Playwright as on main, gofmt, go vet.",
