     "body": "The Routing page shows no hit rate for a request whose plugin said `magpie_cache_unknown`. Kiro caches on its side but returns no token counts, cache included. opencode-kiro-auth 0.1.16 now says so, where it used to say 0 (zeewell on X).\n\nThe usage ledger doesn't carry that flag yet. `usage.Record` has no field for it, and the gateway's `Usage.cacheUnknown` reaches only `RouteUsage.CacheUnknown`. So the ledger's aggregate hit rates still count a Kiro prompt as a miss:\n\n- Usage page, \"Cache hit rate\" block: `internal/gui/assets/plugins/usage/page.js`, around line 1120.\n- Ledger totals: `internal/gui/assets/app.js`, `blk(\"Cache hit rate\", …)`, around line 16947.\n\nA ledger filtered to Kiro shows 0%. A mixed ledger's rate is diluted by every Kiro prompt.\n\nFix: carry the flag into `usage.Record` as a row flag (check for a free bit: 256 and 512 are taken). Leave flagged rows out of the hit rate's numerator and denominator, as the Routing page's `promptOf` does now, and say how many requests the rate covers.\n\nLeft alone in the commit that added `magpie_cache_unknown` to the gateway and the Routing page.\n",
