   "body": "Follow-up delivered on `fix/sessions-day-cache-unknown` ([4264a4b7](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/4264a4b7), on top of the first half [fe330ea1](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/fe330ea1) cherry-picked as this branch's base — same issue, one dependency): the open remainder is closed.\n\nThe totals tile's rate read `cache_unknown` out of its denominator, but its sum came from the stats' day rows — and a native session's day rows carried none, so its Kiro prompts still counted as misses there while the list row showed the true rate. The stats join the amount back from the kept projection per day now (`usage.NativeSessionUnknownByDay`), onto the row of the day, agent and folder the calls were made under; a day the file counted nothing on (its calls were the unknown ones alone, or a zone boundary moved them) gets a row of its own, whose empty model no filter lists. The tile sums `cache_unknown` with the rest. A gateway-only session's days already carried it — joined once, not twice.\n\nRed before: a native session with Kiro calls of 400 and 500 on two days beside a gateway-only one of 700 carried 0 of cache_unknown on its days (denominator kept all 1,600); after, 1,600, each call once. `go test ./internal/gui ./internal/sessions ./internal/usage -count=1` green; sessions-overview Playwright as on main.",
